segments.translation_html:
Number, characteristics, sequence;
Definition, good qualities to be acquainted with;
Classification, summary, opposites;
Good qualities, and certainty of interconnections.

The four reliances are:
- Mental involvement in being interested in the profound scriptures that teach the six perfections;
- Mental involvement in wishing to taste the good qualities of the view arising from meditating on the six perfections;
- Mental involvement in rejoicing in the practice of the six perfections in this world of existence;
- Mental involvement in joyfully anticipating the future arising of the good qualities of the six perfections for oneself and others.

The wisdom of application is engagement in non-conceptual thought;
The wisdom of abiding is the main practice;
The wisdom of fulfillment is the off-session practice.
Thus there are three types of wisdom.

By giving, acquire wealth; by discipline, happiness;
By patience, a noble form; by diligence, dignity;
By meditation, peace; by intellect, liberation.
By compassion, all purposes will be accomplished.
